-- pre-epoch (Unix seconds)
1000-01-01 00:00:00.000
-- post-epoch (Unix seconds)
3000-01-01 00:00:00.000
-- seconds written at precision 0 still decode at precision 3
2020-01-01 00:00:00.000
-- default output truncates subseconds to Unix seconds
2020-01-01 00:00:00.000
-- documented upper bound at precision 7 (scaled ticks)
9999-12-31 23:59:59.9999999
-- past upper bound at precision 7 (errs)
-- scaled ticks near the Unix epoch require a matching precision
1970-01-01 00:00:20.5555555
-- scaled ticks for a regular timestamp require a matching precision
2024-06-15 12:34:56.123456
-- output scale must match the column precision (errs)
-- input scale must match the column precision (errs)
-- reading ticks into a different column precision is rejected (errs)
-- matching ticks preserve subseconds
2020-01-01 00:00:00.123
-- scale 0 ticks are Unix seconds
2020-01-01 00:00:00
-- scale outside the DateTime64 range is rejected (errs)
-- double field stores fractional Unix seconds (independent of the scale setting)
-- double read preserves subseconds without the scale setting
2020-01-01 00:00:00.125
-- double write preserves subseconds without the scale setting
1577836800.125
-- fractional double 1.5 is Unix seconds, not truncated ticks
1970-01-01 00:00:01.500
